-### Hard Voxelization (Non-Deterministic)
-A faster, non-reproducible variant of hard voxelization that uses atomic operations or parallel reductions to assign points to voxels, avoiding the sorting/unique step of the deterministic version [S3, unofficial]. It filters out invalid coordinates, finds unique voxel coordinates using `at::unique_dim`, and then uses `nondisterministic_get_assign_pos` and `nondisterministic_assign_point_voxel` kernels to assign features [S3, unofficial]. It is faster but not reproducible. Choose this when speed is prioritized over reproducibility [S3, unofficial].
