+### [Voxel Hashing and Mean Aggregation](11234-voxel-hashing-and-mean-aggregation.md)
+This method converts a set of 3D points into a sparse voxel grid by mapping points to unique voxel identifiers via hashing and aggregating features using mean scattering. It differs from fixed-grid approaches by avoiding pre-allocated dense memory for empty space, instead dynamically allocating only for occupied voxels. It is chosen when memory efficiency for sparse point clouds is critical and mean aggregation is the desired feature reduction strategy.
